{
  "evaluation": "All three correctly treat both findings as on-question and select genuine disagreement with population as the primary reason, while noting that Study B does not establish a harmful direction. C is strongest because it clearly distinguishes the reported significance from the unsupported direction and identifies the population, design, and outcome differences without overinterpretation. B is close, though classifying dietary intake versus serum measurement as an intervention difference is less clear-cut. A is also sound, but its emphasis on a small cohort adds little: sample size alone does not establish underpowering or explain the disagreement.",
  "ranking": ["C", "B", "A"]
}
